# ==========================================
# INITIALIZATION
# ==========================================
set {cold_meter} = 0

[background arg="res://Assets/scene 1 eyes closed.png" fade="1.0"]
[voice path="res://Audio/prologue1 - 1st line.mp3" volume="0.0"]

I used to hold you when you told me about your dreams. The ones where I died.
[background arg="res://Assets/scene 1 eyes open.png" fade="1.0"]
[voice path="res://Audio/prologue1 - 2nd line.mp3" volume="0.0"]
Tragic. Sudden. Always so vivid.
[background arg="res://Assets/scene 1 eyes closed.png" fade="1.0"]
[voice path="res://Audio/prologue1 - 3rd line.mp3" volume="0.0"]
You’d wake up in a panic, and I’d press your head to my chest and whisper\: "I’m not going anywhere."
[background arg="res://Assets/scene 1 eyes open.png" fade="1.0"]
[voice path="res://Audio/prologue1 - 4th line.mp3" volume="0.0"]
But your dreams became my reality. Only in mine... you're the one burning.

[background arg="res://Assets/blackscreen.png" fade="2.0"]
[background arg="res://Assets/bedroom.png" fade="2.0"]

audio "res://Audio/fire.mp3"
join character1 (Sad) left

character1 (Surprised): Fire...
character1 (covering mouth): I have to wake you up! The air is already impossible to breathe.

[signal arg="start_timer_fire"]

- Call his name
    # Tells the Godot engine to stop the timer because the player clicked
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    set {cold_meter} -= 5
    character1 (Surprised): Wake up! Please, don't leave me here!
    jump continuation_scene_1
- Shake him hard
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    set {cold_meter} += 5
    character1 (desperate): Shaking him desperately Come on, move! We have to get out!
    jump continuation_scene_1

label panic_paralysis
# Godot forcefully jumps the player here if the 5 seconds run out
set {cold_meter} -= 15
character1 (coughing): Frozen in fear, coughing I... I can't move. The smoke is too thick. I'm wasting time just staring at him!

label continuation_scene_1
He won't wake up. Maybe he never wanted to.
The smoke burns my lungs. The ceiling is starting to cave in.

- Try to lift him (You can't leave him)
    set {cold_meter} -= 10
    character1 (coughing): Coughing violently No... I can't carry you. You're too heavy. You were always too heavy to carry.
- Save yourself (Leave him behind)
    set {cold_meter} += 15
    character1 (desperate): Coughing You've dragged me down enough.
    I look at him one last time.
    character1 (Sad): I'm sorry.

The ceiling collapses right next to the bed. A wall of flames cuts us apart.
leave character1

The fire has swallowed the door. The stairs are a death trap.
The only way out is the window. The only way is to jump.
[background arg="res://Assets/blackscreen.png" fade="1.0"]

[background arg="res://Assets/bedroom2.png" fade="2.0"]
join character1 (scared) center

I wake up gasping. The bedroom is freezing.

[background arg="res://Assets/bedroom3.png" fade="2.0"]
His jacket is on the chair in the corner. It's been there since the night he slammed the door.
The ceiling is the same. The jacket is the same. I'm the one who has to change.

# TIMER 2: The Jacket (5 seconds)
[signal arg="start_timer_jacket"]

- Put the jacket on
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    jump choice_jacket_on
- Leave it on the chair
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    jump choice_jacket_leave

label choice_jacket_on
set {cold_meter} -= 5
[background arg="res://Assets/nojacket.png" fade="2.0"]
character1 (neutral_jacket): I put it on. It's too big. Always too big.
The smell of cigarette smoke is still in the fabric. It makes me cough.
jump outside_transition

label choice_jacket_leave
set {cold_meter} += 5
[background arg="res://Assets/door.png" fade="2.0"]
I walk past it toward the door. I'll throw it away later. Or tomorrow.
But I walked past it, and that's all that matters right now.
jump outside_transition

label outside_transition

leave character1

[background arg="res://Assets/outdoor.png" fade="1.0"]

join character1 left

audio "res://Audio/ruins.mp3"
I'm out. The cold is real, but at least the air is clean. It doesn't smell like ash.

label outside_hub
if {investigated_objects} >= 2:
    jump bravery_chapter

audio "res://Audio/shadows.mp3"
[background arg="res://Assets/objects.png" fade="1.0"]
What should I look at?

- The Dead Plant | [if {plant_checked} == false]
    [background arg="res://Assets/plant.png" fade="1.0"]
    set {plant_checked} = true
    set {investigated_objects} += 1
    He bought it saying we'd take care of something together. I kept it alive for months, until I got tired.
    - Water the dry soil
        set {cold_meter} -= 5
        I don't know if it will come back. I pour water over the dry roots anyway.
    - Throw the pot away
        set {cold_meter} += 5
        It's not my fault some things aren't meant to survive. I push it. It shatters.
    jump outside_hub

- The Mailbox | [if {mailbox_checked} == false]
    [background arg="res://Assets/mailbox.png" fade="1.0"]
    set {mailbox_checked} = true
    set {investigated_objects} += 1
    An unsent letter I wrote weeks before the breakup. Full of apologies for things that weren't my fault.
    - Tear it to pieces
        set {cold_meter} += 5
        I don't owe him any more apologies. The paper flutters into the winter wind.
    - Put it back
        set {cold_meter} -= 5
        Maybe I still want him to read it. Maybe I still want him to forgive me.
    jump outside_hub

- The Old Bicycle | [if {bike_checked} == false]
    [background arg="res://Assets/bike.png" fade="1.0"]
    set {bike_checked} = true
    set {investigated_objects} += 1
    Still chained to the railing. Tire flat. It reminds me of the summers before the silence took over.
    - Kick the tire
        set {cold_meter} += 5
        It's just junk now. Rusting in my space.
    - Touch the handle
        set {cold_meter} -= 5
        The metal freezes my fingertips. I remember how his hands felt when they started growing cold toward me.
    jump outside_hub

# ==========================================
# THE DISCOMFORT & BRAVERY
# ==========================================
label bravery_chapter

leave character1

[background arg="res://Assets/blackscreen.png" fade="1.0"]

join character1 left

audio "res://Audio/after.mp3"
Everything hurts. I think that's progress. The numbness is cracking. I'm tired, cold, and for the first time since the jump, fully present.

I used to think discomfort meant something was wrong. Now I think it might mean something is still alive.
character1: I don't know if this is healing. But I'm doing things again. That has to count for something.

[background arg="res://Assets/street.png" fade="1.0"]
The world feels wider here. I move further from the house than I have before.

I reach a place I used to go alone.
- Stay for a second
    set {cold_meter} += 5
    It's still here. So am I.
- Walk past
    set {cold_meter} -= 5
    I notice it, but I keep walking. I'm not ready yet.

[background arg="res://Assets/sun.png" fade="2.0"]
Suddenly, the sun breaks through the clouds. A small, unexpected warmth hits my face.

# TIMER 3: Good Moment (5 seconds)
[signal arg="start_timer_moment"]

- Let yourself feel it
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    jump choice_moment_feel
- Shut it down
    [signal arg="stop_timer"]
    jump choice_moment_shut

label choice_moment_feel
set {cold_meter} += 5
I let it land. Just for a second. I don't think about him.
jump void_chapter

label choice_moment_shut
set {cold_meter} -= 5
I don't deserve a good moment yet. Not while things are still like this.
jump void_chapter

# ==========================================
# THE VOID
# ==========================================
[background arg="res://Assets/blackscreen.png" fade="2.0"]
label void_chapter
character1: I keep waiting for the moment it stops hurting. I think that might not be how it works. I think you just get better at carrying it.
I thought getting better would feel like something. Mostly it just feels like nothing. I'm trying to decide if that's okay.

[background arg="res://Assets/phone.png" fade="2.0"]
My phone vibrates. An old message from him saved in the archive.
- Delete it
    set {cold_meter} += 10
    I don't read it first. If I read it first I won't delete it.
- Read it, put it down
    set {cold_meter} -= 5
    It says something kind. That's almost worse than if it said something cruel.
- Read it and reply
    [background arg="res://Assets/type.png" fade="2.0"]
    set {cold_meter} -= 15
    I type something. I don't send it. I type it again. I still don't send it.

[background arg="res://Assets/street.png" fade="1.0"]
label void_house_choice
I find myself looking down the street that leads back to the house.

- Keep walking forward
    [background arg="res://Assets/downstreet.png" fade="1.0"]
    set {cold_meter} += 10
    Not today. I have somewhere to be. I don't. But I pretend I do, and somewhere along the way it becomes true.
    jump evaluate_endings
- Turn back to the house
    [background arg="res://Assets/return.png" fade="1.0"]
    set {cold_meter} -= 15
    I don't know why I'm going back. I think I just need to see it.
    jump the_return

# ==========================================
# THE RETURN
# ==========================================
label the_return
Something inside me keeps trying to turn around.

[background arg="res://Assets/closeddoor.png" fade="2.0"]
I reach the door. I turn the handle.

leave character1

jump evaluate_endings

# ==========================================
# ENDINGS EVALUATION
# ==========================================
label evaluate_endings

if {cold_meter} <= -20:
    jump ending_1_intrusive_memory
if {cold_meter} >= 20:
    jump ending_2_acceptance
else:
    jump ending_3_the_walk

# --- ENDING 1 ---
label ending_1_intrusive_memory
[background arg="res://Assets/bedroom.png" fade="1.0"]

join character1 left

She goes back inside. The cycle continues.
The air suddenly becomes suffocating. The ground beneath my feet is burning.

The fire in the dream wasn't an accident. We were the fire. We burned each other until there was nothing left.
character1: You've been here before.

leave character1
[background arg="res://Assets/ending1.png" fade="1.0"]
[end_timeline]

# --- ENDING 2 ---
label ending_2_acceptance
[background arg="res://Assets/bench.png" fade="2.0"]

join character1 left

I look down near the bench in the yard. I notice something shining in the grass.
[background arg="res://Assets/watch.png" fade="2.0"]
I pick it up. It's my old watch. Scratched. Stopped at a time I don't recognise.
But it's mine.
The cold is still here, but it doesn't freeze me anymore.

leave character1
[background arg="res://Assets/ending2.png" fade="1.0"]
[end_timeline]

# --- ENDING 3 ---
label ending_3_the_walk
[background arg="res://Assets/downstreet.png" fade="2.0"]

join character1 left

She doesn't go back into the house. She keeps walking.
The street stretches out in front of me.
character1: I don't know where I'm going. That's the first time that's felt okay.

[background arg="res://Assets/ending3.png" fade="1.0"]
leave character1
[end_timeline]